__pycache__
*.lock
.env
.coverage
# pytest-xdist writes one per worker: .coverage.<host>.<pid>.<rand>
.coverage.*

# Local virtualenv + test runner caches.
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Per-machine Claude Code permission grants - gitignored by convention.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Isolated per-session working clones for parallel Claude sessions (see CLAUDE.md "Parallel
# sessions"). Each is a full `git clone` of this repo, kept out of git so the two working trees
# never cross-contaminate. Lives on the host mount, so it survives a container rebuild.
.clones/

# /diagram POOL - TWO TREES WITH OPPOSITE POLICIES, which is why these rules are patterns rather
# than the 49 hand-written lines they replaced (feature 161).
#
#   pool/<tier>/<map>/            LIVE. Regenerated and re-gated every run, so every render is
#                                 DERIVED and ignored - a to-scale .svg is tens of MB (one
#                                 primitive per crop row) and rebuilds on demand with
#                                 `make map GEN=pool/<tier>/<map>/<map>.gen.py`.
#   legacy-hand-authored-pool/    FROZEN exhibits (GM 2026-08-16). Their gens are never re-run, so
#                                 once the engine drifted their renders stopped being reproducible:
#                                 they are historical artifacts nothing can faithfully rebuild, and
#                                 are therefore COMMITTED write-once (~195 MB, one time - they can
#                                 never change again). NOTHING here is ignored; that is the whole
#                                 rule, and it is why the 36 per-file `!` un-ignore lines this
#                                 block used to carry are gone.
#
# Before the split the two policies were interleaved in one directory, so each exhibit had to be
# exempted BY NAME. Separating the trees turned a per-file exemption list into a per-tree rule.
# WHEN A MAP IS CONVERTED to scripted generation it MOVES TREES (git mv into pool/), and its
# renders become derived and ignored automatically - no ignore line to add or delete either way.
#
# The one exception inside the live tree: a Mode A compound plan has no generator that draws it
# from data - its .svg IS the source, KB-sized - so magistracy .svg stays tracked and only its .png
# is derived.
.claude/skills/diagram/pool/*/*/*.svg
.claude/skills/diagram/pool/*/*/*.png
.claude/skills/diagram/pool/*/*/*.html
!.claude/skills/diagram/pool/magistracies/*/*.svg
# The pool's browsable index - derived from the manifests/notes by pool_index.py and rewritten by
# render-sync (render_cache.py) so it stays current in main beside the renders it embeds.
.claude/skills/diagram/pool/index.html

# Spoiler-sensitive /dream scenes: the local tier is the GM's disk only, never committed.
# The public tier (.claude/skills/dream/pool/) stays tracked; see that skill's SKILL.md.
.claude/skills/dream/pool-local/

# GNOME atomic-save temp files (a stray one was once committed); never track these.
.goutputstream-*

# Generated org chart - rebuild with `webapp/orgchart.py --format png` rather than tracking it.
webapp/orgchart.png
top_up-improvement.md

# DRAFT maps parked outside pool/ (see .claude/skills/diagram/wip/README.md): a map that is not
# yet green cannot live in pool/, because test_villages.py sweeps pool/*/*.gen.py and would turn
# `make done` red for every session. Its derived render is ignored exactly like a pool render.
# A SINGLE `*` DOES NOT CROSS `/` (feature 173): `wip/shiro-daika.gen.py` became the
# `wip/shiro_daika/` package, its render moved one directory down, and these four patterns
# silently stopped matching - 8.7 MB of derived PNG/SVG/JSON/HTML landed in a commit before
# the settlement-review caught it. The `**` forms cover any depth wip/ grows to next.
.claude/skills/diagram/wip/*.svg
.claude/skills/diagram/wip/**/*.svg
.claude/skills/diagram/wip/*.png
.claude/skills/diagram/wip/**/*.png
.claude/skills/diagram/wip/*.json
.claude/skills/diagram/wip/**/*.json

# Spec-kit's ACTIVE-FEATURE pointer - per-workspace state, never shared. It was tracked until
# 2026-08-16, when a peer session's /speckit-specify commit repointed it mid-chain and the merge
# handed this session the OTHER feature's directory. That is not cosmetic: spec-kit resolves
# FEATURE_DIR from this file at priority 2, ABOVE the SPECIFY_FEATURE env var (priority 3), so a
# stale pointer silently redirects setup-plan.sh / setup-tasks.sh / implement into a peer's
# specs/NNN-*/ while CURRENT_BRANCH still reads correctly. Each clone writes its own; nothing
# shares it. See CLAUDE.md 'Concurrent sessions' and scripts/clone-sync-hooks.sh's re-track guard.
.specify/feature.json

# feature 130: the AWS/GitHub credentials the CodeBuild dispatcher reads (see development-secrets.ini.example)
development-secrets.ini
# feature 129: raw cProfile output stays out of this repository (FR-011a); the derived table is committed
.claude/skills/diagram/dev/perf-raw/
.claude/skills/diagram/wip/*.html
.claude/skills/diagram/wip/**/*.html
